WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.227
This code one-hot encodes the nominal variable sex.

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:09.397
The goal is to represent categories without assigning them a single numerical rank.

00:00:09.397 --> 00:00:11.062
With drop first, one category becomes the reference.

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:20.212
Handle unknown provides a defined behavior if a later dataset contains a category not seen during fitting.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:25.552
The key idea is that the encoding follows from the nominal meaning of the variable.

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:31.587
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:36.817
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:44.522
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:44.522 --> 00:00:45.740
floating-point number.
